-- title:
--   Horizontal primes at depth p/q counted by the index drop
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, let $e \ge 1$ and $q \ge 1$ be natural numbers, and write $R =$ `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)` for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \varpi^{e}$. Let $x \in R$ be nonzero and let $(a,b)$ be a pair of one-variable power series over $W$ with $b$ of zero constant term such that $x$ is the class of $\mathrm{inU}(a) + \mathrm{inV}(b)$, where $\mathrm{inU}(a)$ has coefficient $a_i$ on the monomials $X_0^i$ and zero elsewhere and $\mathrm{inV}(b)$ has coefficient $b_j$ on $X_1^j$ and zero elsewhere. Let $p \ge 1$ satisfy $p + 1 \le qe$. Then the (unordered, finitely supported) sum over those primes $\mathfrak{P}$ of $R$ with $\mathfrak{P} \ne 0$, with the class `const (ϖ ^ e) ϖ` of the constant $\varpi$ not in $\mathfrak{P}$, and with $q \cdot \operatorname{length}_W\bigl(R/(\mathfrak{P} + (\,$`U (ϖ ^ e)`$\,))\bigr) = p \cdot \operatorname{rank}_W(R/\mathfrak{P})$ in $\mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$, of the products $\operatorname{rank}_W(R/\mathfrak{P}) \cdot \operatorname{length}_{R_{\mathfrak{P}}}\bigl((R/xR)_{\mathfrak{P}}\bigr)$, equals `circleIndexDrop` of $(a,b)$ for the scaled valuation $w \mapsto q\cdot \mathrm{addVal}_W(w)$ with parameters $E = qe$ and $t = p$, that is, the difference $\sup D - \inf D$, truncated to $\mathbb{N}$, of the set $D$ of integers $n$ at which `termOrder` for these data agrees with `repGaussOrder` of $\mathrm{inU}(a) + \mathrm{inV}(b)$.
--
--   This is the interior slope law for the width-$e$ crossing model: on the circle of depth $p/q$ of the annulus $0 \le v(U) \le e$, the zeros of $x$ — the horizontal primes of $R$ (nonzero, not containing $\varpi$) whose depth invariant is $p/q$, counted with $W$-rank and with the local multiplicity of $x$ — are as many as the drop between the largest and smallest dominant index of the normal form $a(U) + b(V)$ at that depth, an algebraic form of Weierstrass preparation on a circle. It is used in the study of prolongation tuples for place specialisations, where the slope drop of a tuple is expressed as a sum over depths.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_finsum_rank_mul_length_eq_circleIndexDrop.lean

